cff-version: 1.2.0
title: SADI Go/No-Go dissection zone annotation platform
message: >-
  If you use this software in research, please cite it. The licence covers the
  software only, never the surgical frames or the annotations produced with it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: SADI Go/No-Go study contributors
    # Replace with the named authors before publication.
repository-code: https://github.com/SoRRad/GoNoGo
abstract: >-
  A web application for collecting independent Go and No-Go dissection zone
  annotations from multiple surgeons on still frames from robotic duodenal
  switch procedures. Surgeons draw zones on a hand-written pointer-event canvas,
  masks are stored per surgeon at native resolution and never merged, and the
  export reports inter-rater agreement (IoU, Dice, normalised surface distance,
  chance-corrected presence agreement) alongside intra-rater reliability
  measured from hidden repeated frames.
keywords:
  - surgical data science
  - inter-rater reliability
  - image annotation
  - duodenal switch
  - SADI-S
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-09-17'
